  "title": "Vanishing product-tested α-derivative forces a.e. constant slices (fibrewise du Bois-Reymond)",
  "statement": "Let a, b, c, d ∈ ℝ with c < d, I := (a, b), J := (c, d), and let H : ℝ × ℝ → ℝ be Lebesgue integrable on I × J. Assume ∫_{ℝ×ℝ} ψ'(α)·l(t)·H(t, α) d(t, α) = 0 for all ψ, l ∈ C¹(ℝ) with tsupport ψ ⊆ J and tsupport l ⊆ I, where ψ' = deriv ψ. Then for almost every t ∈ I there is k ∈ ℝ with H(t, α) = k for almost every α ∈ J.",
  "lean_statement": "∀ (a b c d : ℝ) (H : ℝ × ℝ → ℝ), c < d → IntegrableOn H (Ioo a b ×ˢ Ioo c d) → (∀ ψ l : ℝ → ℝ, ContDiff ℝ 1 ψ → ContDiff ℝ 1 l → tsupport ψ ⊆ Ioo c d → tsupport l ⊆ Ioo a b → ∫ p : ℝ × ℝ, deriv ψ p.2 * l p.1 * H p = 0) → ∀ᵐ t, t ∈ Ioo a b → ∃ k : ℝ, ∀ᵐ α, α ∈ Ioo c d → H (t, α) = k",
